When the user's message names the files to deliver, present exactly those — no others and none missing — even if this turn changed more. Otherwise, in this project the work itself is the deliverable: every file this turn created or modified inside the project directory — source code, scripts, configuration, data, documents, images, audio or video, archives; no kind of file is excluded. Do not present a file this turn did not change, a deleted file, or a file created only to have something to present. Call it once, after the files are final, listing every deliverable; each one gets a download and preview card. Paths must be inside the project directory — save or copy a deliverable there first if it was written elsewhere. Presenting the same path again later records a new version.
